# Line endings are declared here rather than left to each user's global core.autocrlf.
#
# Without this file the committed blobs are LF while a Windows working tree is CRLF, so
# a clone on Linux or macOS with core.autocrlf=false - the default there, and what a CI
# runner gets - reports every tracked text file as modified immediately after cloning:
# 168 files and 63,788 insertions against 63,788 deletions, with no real change in any
# of them. This project reads "local and remote agree" off `git status` as part of its
# verification, so that signal has to mean the same thing on every machine
# (final audit A-01).

*               text=auto eol=lf

# Data and documents are compared byte-for-byte against the retrieval manifest and, for
# figures, against previous builds. Nothing may rewrite their bytes.
*.png           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.htm           binary
*.html          binary
*.bundle        binary

# CSV is text and normalises safely, but the committed tables are checked for
# byte-identical reproduction, so pin the ending explicitly rather than inferring it.
*.csv           text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.toml          text eol=lf
*.txt           text eol=lf
Makefile        text eol=lf
